{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CCUpUtgvhMnQbDHzWj8KGp","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→defmodule LiveVite.E2E.ReactEventLive do\n     2→  @moduledoc false\n     3→  use Phoenix.LiveView\n     4→\n     5→  def mount(_params, _session, socket) do\n     6→    {:ok, assign(socket, message: \"\", event_count: 0)}\n     7→  end\n     8→\n     9→  def handle_event(\"send_notification\", %{\"message\" => message}, socket) do\n    10→    send(self(), {:broadcast_event, \"notification\", %{message: message, timestamp: :os.system_time(:millisecond)}})\n    11→    {:noreply, assign(socket, message: message, event_count: socket.assigns.event_count + 1)}\n    12→  end\n    13→\n    14→  def handle_event(\"send_custom_event\", %{\"data\" => data}, socket) do\n    15→    send(self(), {:broadcast_event, \"custom_event\", %{data: data, count: socket.assigns.event_count + 1}})\n    16→    {:noreply, assign(socket, event_count: socket.assigns.event_count + 1)}\n    17→  end\n    18→\n    19→  def handle_info({:broadcast_event, event_name, payload}, socket) do\n    20→    {:noreply, push_event(socket, event_name, payload)}\n    21→  end\n    22→\n    23→  def render(assigns) do\n    24→    ~H\"\"\"\n    25→    <div id=\"react-event-test\">\n    26→      <div id=\"message-display\">Message: {@message}</div>\n    27→      <div id=\"event-count\">Event Count: {@event_count}</div>\n    28→      <LiveVite.react message={@message} event_count={@event_count} v-component=\"event_test\" v-socket={@socket} />\n    29→    </div>\n    30→    \"\"\"\n    31→  end\n    32→end\n    33→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"t