{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015ojvdVRoouvGsKTr62riCu","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→defmodule LiveVite.E2E.ReactStreamLive do\n     2→  @moduledoc false\n     3→  use Phoenix.LiveView\n     4→\n     5→  def render(assigns) do\n     6→    ~H\"\"\"\n     7→    <div id=\"react-stream-test\">\n     8→      <LiveVite.react items={@streams.items} v-component=\"stream_test\" v-socket={@socket} />\n     9→    </div>\n    10→    \"\"\"\n    11→  end\n    12→\n    13→  def mount(_params, _session, socket) do\n    14→    items = [\n    15→      %{id: 1, name: \"Item 1\", description: \"First item\"},\n    16→      %{id: 2, name: \"Item 2\", description: \"Second item\"},\n    17→      %{id: 3, name: \"Item 3\", description: \"Third item\"}\n    18→    ]\n    19→\n    20→    socket =\n    21→      socket\n    22→      |> stream_configure(:items, dom_id: &\"songs-#{&1.id}\")\n    23→      |> stream(:items, items)\n    24→      |> assign(:next_id, 4)\n    25→\n    26→    {:ok, socket}\n    27→  end\n    28→\n    29→  def handle_event(\"add_item\", %{\"name\" => name, \"description\" => description}, socket) do\n    30→    new_item = %{\n    31→      id: socket.assigns.next_id,\n    32→      name: name,\n    33→      description: description\n    34→    }\n    35→\n    36→    socket =\n    37→      socket\n    38→      |> stream_insert(:items, new_item)\n    39→      |> assign(:next_id, socket.assigns.next_id + 1)\n    40→\n    41→    {:noreply, socket}\n    42→  end\n    43→\n    44→  def handle_event(\"remove_item\", %{\"id\" => id}, socket) do\n    45→    {:noreply, stream_delete_by_dom_id(socket, :items, \"songs-#{id}\")}\n    46→  end\n    47→\n    48→  def handle_event(\"clear_stream\", _params, socket) do\n    49→    socket =\n    50→      socket\n    51→      |> stream(:items, [], reset: true)\n    52→      |> assign(:next_id, 1)\n    53→\n    54→    {:noreply, socket}\n    55→  end\n    56→\n    57→  def handle_event(\"reset_stream\", _params, socket) do\n    58→    items = [\n    59→      %{id: 1, name: \"Item 1\", description: \"First item\"},\n    60→      %{id: 2, name: \"Item 2\", description: \"Second item\"},\n    61→      %{id: 3, name: \"Item 3\", description: \"Third item\"}\n    62→    ]\n    63→\n    64→    socket =\n    65→      socket\n    66→      |> stream(:items, items, at: -1, reset: true)\n    67→      |> assign(:next_id, 4)\n    68→\n    69→    {:noreply, socket}\n    70→  end\n    71→\n    72→  def handle_event(\"reset_stream_at_0\", _params, socket) do\n    73→    items = [\n    74→      %{id: 1, name: \"Item 1\", description: \"First item\"},\n    75→      %{id: 2, name: \"Item 2\", description: \"Second item\"},\n    76→      %{id: 3, name: \"Item 3\", description: \"Third item\"}\n    77→    ]\n    78→\n    79→    socket =\n    80→      socket\n    81→      |> stream(:items, items, at: 0, reset: true)\n    82→      |> assign(:next_id, 4)\n    83→\n    84→    {:noreply, socket}\n    85→  end\n    86→\n    87→  def handle_event(\"add_multiple_start\", _params, socket) do\n    88→    new_items = [\n    89→      %{id: socket.assigns.next_id, name: \"Start Item A\", description: \"Added at start A\"},\n    90→      %{id: socket.assigns.next_id + 1, name: \"Start Item B\", description: \"Added at start B\"},\n    91→      %{id: socket.assigns.next_id + 2, name: \"Start Item C\", description: \"Added at start C\"}\n    92→    ]\n    93→\n    94→    socket =\n    95→      socket\n    96→      |> stream(:items, new_items, at: 0, limit: 5)\n    97→      |> assign(:next_id, socket.assigns.next_id + 3)\n    98→\n    99→    {:noreply, socket}\n   100→  end\n   101→\n   102→  def handle_event(\"add_multiple_end\", _params, socket) do\n   103→    new_items = [\n   104→      %{id: socket.assigns.next_id, name: \"End Item X\", description: \"Added at end X\"},\n   105→      %{id: socket.assigns.next_id + 1, name: \"End Item Y\", description: \"Added at end Y\"},\n   106→      %{id: socket.assigns.next_id + 2, name: \"End Item Z\", description: \"Added at end Z\"}\n   107→    ]\n   108→\n   109→    socket =\n   110→      socket\n   111→      |> stream(:items, new_items, at: -1, limit: -5)\n   112→      |> assign(:next_id, socket.assigns.next_id + 3)\n   113→\n   114→    {:noreply, socket}\n   115→  end\n   116→\n   117→  def handle_event(\"add_with_positive_limit\", %{\"limit\" => limit_str}, socket) do\n   118→    limit = String.to_integer(limit_str)\n   119→\n   120→    new_item = %{\n   121→      id: socket.assigns.next_id,\n   122→      name: \"Limited Item +#{limit}\",\n   123→      description: \"Added with positive limit #{limit}\"\n   124→    }\n   125→\n   126→    socket =\n   127→      socket\n   128→      |> stream_insert(:items, new_item, at: 0, limit: limit)\n   129→      |> assign(:next_id, socket.assigns.next_id + 1)\n   130→\n   131→    {:noreply, socket}\n   132→  end\n   133→\n   134→  def handle_event(\"add_with_negative_limit\", %{\"limit\" => limit_str}, socket) do\n   135→    limit = String.to_integer(limit_str) * -1\n   136→\n   137→    new_item = %{\n   138→      id: socket.assigns.next_id,\n   139→      name: \"Limited Item #{limit}\",\n   140→      description: \"Added with negative limit #{limit}\"\n   141→    }\n   142→\n   143→    socket =\n   144→      socket\n   145→      |> stream_insert(:items, new_item, limit: limit)\n   146→      |> assign(:next_id, socket.assigns.next_id + 1)\n   147→\n   148→    {:noreply, socket}\n   149→  end\n   150→end\n   151→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01AR1i2yA9m6AgxHk4DLHmVE","session_id":"e05a5f27-3808-43b9-9b1f-a81d138cf285","uuid":"9fc792f5-a62f-4457-b5b3-ec3a8100c558"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01VD8i5zxenYaSq9XyENcoZB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015vGna8r5rWCzUMYM3Pygoa","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/test/e2e/features/react-stream/stream_test.tsx"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":27396,"cache_read_input_tokens":18926,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":27396},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01AR1i2yA9m6AgxHk4DLHmVE","session_id":"e05a5f27-3808-43b9-9b1f-a81d138cf285","uuid":"635c6757-c6c0-483d-8f6a-df90602d16fd"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015vGna8r5rWCzUMYM3Pygoa","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→import { useState } from \"react\"\n     2→import { useLive } from \"live_vite\"\n     3→\n     4→interface Item {\n     5→  id: number\n     6→  name: string\n     7→  description: string\n     8→}\n     9→\n    10→export default function StreamTest({ items }: { items: Item[] }) {\n    11→  const live = useLive()\n    12→  const [newItem, setNewItem] = useState({ name: \"\", description: \"\" })\n    13→  const [positiveLimit, setPositiveLimit] = useState(3)\n    14→  const [negativeLimit, setNegativeLimit] = useState(3)\n    15→\n    16→  const addItem = () => {\n    17→    if (!newItem.name.trim()) {\n    18→      alert(\"Please enter a name for the item\")\n    19→      return\n    20→    }\n    21→    live.pushEvent(\"add_item\", { name: newItem.name, description: newItem.description })\n    22→    setNewItem({ name: \"\", description: \"\" })\n    23→  }\n    24→\n    25→  const removeItem = (id: number) => {\n    26→    live.pushEvent(\"remove_item\", { id })\n    27→  }\n    28→\n    29→  return (\n    30→    <div id=\"stream-component\">\n    31→      <h2>Stream Test</h2>\n    32→\n    33→      {/* Add new item form */}\n    34→      <div className=\"add-form\">\n    35→        <h3>Add New Item</h3>\n    36→        <input\n    37→          data-testid=\"name-input\"\n    38→          placeholder=\"Item name\"\n    39→          value={newItem.name}\n    40→          onChange={e => setNewItem({ ...newItem, name: e.target.value })}\n    41→        />\n    42→        <input\n    43→          data-testid=\"description-input\"\n    44→          placeholder=\"Item description\"\n    45→          value={newItem.description}\n    46→          onChange={e => setNewItem({ ...newItem, description: e.target.value })}\n    47→        />\n    48→        <button data-testid=\"add-button\" onClick={addItem}>\n    49→          Add Item\n    50→        </button>\n    51→      </div>\n    52→\n    53→      {/* Stream controls */}\n    54→      <div className=\"stream-controls\">\n    55→        <button data-testid=\"clear-button\" onClick={() => live.pushEvent(\"clear_stream\", {})}>\n    56→          Clear All\n    57→        </button>\n    58→        <button data-testid=\"reset-button\" onClick={() => live.pushEvent(\"reset_stream\", {})}>\n    59→          Reset to Default\n    60→        </button>\n    61→        <button data-testid=\"reset-button-at-0\" onClick={() => live.pushEvent(\"reset_stream_at_0\", {})}>\n    62→          Reset to Default (at: 0)\n    63→        </button>\n    64→      </div>\n    65→\n    66→      {/* Limit operation controls */}\n    67→      <div className=\"limit-controls\">\n    68→        <h3>Limit Operations</h3>\n    69→        <div className=\"limit-section\">\n    70→          <h4>Multiple Insert Operations</h4>\n    71→          <button\n    72→            data-testid=\"add-multiple-start-button\"\n    73→            className=\"limit-button\"\n    74→            onClick={() => live.pushEvent(\"add_multiple_start\", {})}\n    75→          >\n    76→            Add 3 Items at Start (Limit: Keep First 5)\n    77→          </button>\n    78→          <button\n    79→            data-testid=\"add-multiple-end-button\"\n    80→            className=\"limit-button\"\n    81→            onClick={() => live.pushEvent(\"add_multiple_end\", {})}\n    82→          >\n    83→            Add 3 Items at End (Limit: Keep Last 5)\n    84→          </button>\n    85→        </div>\n    86→\n    87→        <div className=\"limit-section\">\n    88→          <h4>Single Insert with Custom Limits</h4>\n    89→          <div className=\"limit-input-group\">\n    90→            <input\n    91→              type=\"number\"\n    92→              min=\"1\"\n    93→              max=\"10\"\n    94→              data-testid=\"positive-limit-input\"\n    95→              className=\"limit-input\"\n    96→              placeholder=\"Positive limit\"\n    97→              value={positiveLimit}\n    98→              onChange={e => setPositiveLimit(Number(e.target.value))}\n    99→            />\n   100→            <button\n   101→              data-testid=\"add-positive-limit-button\"\n   102→              className=\"limit-button\"\n   103→              disabled={!positiveLimit || positiveLimit < 1}\n   104→              onClick={() => live.pushEvent(\"add_with_positive_limit\", { limit: positiveLimit.toString() })}\n   105→            >\n   106→              Add Item (Keep First {positiveLimit || \"?\"})\n   107→            </button>\n   108→          </div>\n   109→\n   110→          <div className=\"limit-input-group\">\n   111→            <input\n   112→              type=\"number\"\n   113→              min=\"1\"\n   114→              max=\"10\"\n   115→              data-testid=\"negative-limit-input\"\n   116→              className=\"limit-input\"\n   117→              placeholder=\"Negative limit\"\n   118→              value={negativeLimit}\n   119→              onChange={e => setNegativeLimit(Number(e.target.value))}\n   120→            />\n   121→            <button\n   122→              data-testid=\"add-negative-limit-button\"\n   123→              className=\"limit-button\"\n   124→              disabled={!negativeLimit || negativeLimit < 1}\n   125→              onClick={() => live.pushEvent(\"add_with_negative_limit\", { limit: negativeLimit.toString() })}\n   126→            >\n   127→              Add Item (Keep Last {negativeLimit || \"?\"})\n   128→            </button>\n   129→          </div>\n   130→        </div>\n   131→      </div>\n   132→\n   133→      {/* Items list */}\n   134→      <div className=\"items-list\">\n   135→        <h3>Items ({items.length})</h3>\n   136→        {items.length === 0 && (\n   137→          <div data-testid=\"empty-message\" className=\"empty-state\">\n   138→            No items in the stream\n   139→          </div>\n   140→        )}\n   141→        {items.map(item => (\n   142→          <div key={item.id} className=\"item\" data-testid={`item-${item.id}`}>\n   143→            <div className=\"item-content\">\n   144→              <h4 data-testid=\"item-name\">{item.name}</h4>\n   145→              <p data-testid=\"item-description\">{item.description}</p>\n   146→              <small data-testid=\"item-id\">ID: {item.id}</small>\n   147→            </div>\n   148→            <button\n   149→              onClick={() => removeItem(item.id)}\n   150→              data-testid={`remove-${item.id}`}\n   151→              className=\"remove-button\"\n   152→            >\n   153→              Remove\n   154→            </button>\n   155→          </div>\n   156→        ))}\n   157→      </div>\n   158→\n   159→      {/* Debug info */}\n   160→      <div className=\"debug-info\">\n   161→        <h4>Debug Info</h4>\n   162→        <p>Items type: {typeof items}</p>\n   163→        <p>Items length: {items.length}</p>\n   164→        <pre data-testid=\"raw-items\">{JSON.stringify(items, null, 2)}</pre>\n   165→      </div>\n   166→    </div>\n   167→  )\n   168→}\n   169→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01AR1i2yA9m6AgxHk4DLHmVE","session_id":"e05a5f27-3808-43b9-9b1f-a81d138cf285","uuid":"074e6691-8970-4fa9-bf34-2678dcb13c5e"}
