{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011cc2H3gTpJMyjQaAvzq4cr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Vue version uses `watchEffect` to continuously update entry refs. The React version uses `useEffect` with dependency on `uploadConfig.entries`. \n\nThe key difference I notice: The Vue version adds the form to `live.el` (the hook element), while the React version does the same. But the issue might be related to the `phx-submit-loading` class being stuck on a form element that's part of the submit flow.\n\nLet me look at the error more carefully - the issue is that `.phx-submit-loading` has count 1 after clicking upload. This means Phoenix applied `phx-submit-loading` but it never got resolved. This is a known behavior - when a form with `phx-submit` submits, Phoenix adds the class and waits for a response. The upload needs to complete first.\n\nThe problem is likely that the uploads aren't actually completing because the hidden form's submit is correctly triggering a Phoenix form submit, but the upload data isn't getting transferred. Let me look at the error context for more details."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":950,"cache_read_input_tokens":101009,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":950},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e05a5f27-3808-43b9-9b1f-a81d138cf285","uuid":"87138c2e-41d3-4ec1-8721-304351ec0f16"}
