{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01BxiZgghbrR4d7bJG27tMba","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I can see the issue clearly:\n\n- **Vue**: `data-phx-active-refs` = `\"0\"` (correct - entry ref \"0\" is active)\n- **React**: `data-phx-active-refs` = `\"\"` (empty - entries not reflected)\n\nAnd crucially, looking at the React component's `data-props`:\n```json\n\"entries\":[]\n```\n\nBut `data-props-diff` shows:\n```json\n[\"add\",\"/upload/entries/0\",{...entry data...}]\n```\n\nSo the **diff** contains the entry, but the props passed to the React component have `entries: []`. This means the JSON patch diffing system isn't correctly applying the upload entries diff to the React component's props. The entry is being added via a diff operation but the React component sees an empty entries array.\n\nThis is a bug in the React renderer's prop handling for upload configs. The JSON patch isn't being applied to the upload config's entries array. Let me look at how props diffs are applied in the React renderer."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1273,"cache_read_input_tokens":109580,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1273},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e05a5f27-3808-43b9-9b1f-a81d138cf285","uuid":"137bdf3b-3705-4ebf-a34b-cdf343bcfe32"}
