{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01QCP83w2fJLaUKd5wMS6dBS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The auto-upload test shows the file is selected (1 file, \"pending\") but not auto-uploaded - still at 0% and 0 uploaded. This is the same `data-phx-active-refs` issue - for auto uploads, Phoenix needs the active refs set to trigger the preflight and upload automatically.\n\nBut wait - the fix I made should handle this since `patchProps` now creates fresh references. The issue might be timing. The auto-upload path in Phoenix checks `data-phx-auto-upload` attribute and the active refs on the input element. Let me check if the timing is just slightly off - let me increase the wait time in the test.\n\nActually, let me look at the Vue auto-upload test more carefully - it also waits 2000ms. The difference might be that with the Vue reactive system, the `watchEffect` runs synchronously when the config changes, but with React's `useEffect` it runs asynchronously after the render, introducing a small delay.\n\nLet me update the auto-upload test to wait a bit longer."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1371,"cache_read_input_tokens":121401,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1371},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e05a5f27-3808-43b9-9b1f-a81d138cf285","uuid":"2e35f4af-4a3e-4976-8995-15541290468f"}
