 done\n    87→    expect(fileStatus?.includes(\"done\") || uploadedCount?.includes(\"1\")).toBeTruthy()\n    88→  })\n    89→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e05a5f27-3808-43b9-9b1f-a81d138cf285","uuid":"2df7b847-f8e0-4054-8d62-c9b309223fa9","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/test/e2e/features/react-upload/react-upload.spec.js","content":"  test(\"should handle automatic upload (auto_upload: true)\", async ({ page }) => {\n    await page.goto(\"/react-upload/auto\")\n    await syncLV(page)\n\n    // Verify initial state\n    await expect(page.locator(\"#upload-mode\")).toContainText(\"auto\")\n    await expect(page.locator(\"#auto-upload\")).toContainText(\"true\")\n    await expect(page.locator(\"#selected-count\")).toContainText(\"0\")\n    await expect(page.locator(\"#uploaded-count\")).toContainText(\"0\")\n\n    // Upload button should not be visible for auto upload\n    await expect(page.locator(\"#upload-btn\")).not.toBeVisible()\n\n    // Create a test file and simulate file selection\n    const testContent = \"This is test file content for auto upload\"\n    await page.setInputFiles('input[type=\"file\"]', {\n      name: \"test-auto.txt\",\n      mimeType: \"text/plain\",\n      buffer: Buffer.from(testContent),\n    })\n\n    await syncLV(page)\n\n    // For auto upload, file should be uploaded automatically\n    // Wait a bit longer for the auto upload to process\n    await page.waitForTimeout(2000)\n    await syncLV(page)\n\n    // Verify file was selected and processed\n    await expect(page.locator(\"#selected-count\")).toContainText(\"1\")\n    await expect(page.locator(\".file-entry\")).toHaveCount(1)\n\n    // Check if the file was processed (either uploaded or marked as done)\n    const fileStatus = await page.locator(\".file-done\").textContent()\n    const uploadedCount = await page.locator(\"#uploaded-count\").textContent()\n\n    // For auto upload, the file should either be uploaded or marked as done\n    expect(fileStatus?.includes(\"done\") || uploadedCount?.includes(\"1\")).toBeTruthy()\n  })\n","numLines":40,"startLine":50,"totalLines":312}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01QmqQUG2kYrje6kVSjhxisu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The issue with auto-upload is deeper. With auto-upload, Phoenix needs to:\n1. Detect the file selection (change event)\n2. See the entry is active (data-phx-active-refs) \n3. Auto-preflight and upload\n\nBut the `data-phx-active-refs` is updated in a `useEffect` that runs after React renders. By then, Phoenix has already processed the change event. So the auto-upload preflight check happens before the refs are updated.\n\nThis is a fundamental timing issue with the React upload hook. The Vue `watchEffect` runs synchronously when the reactive config changes, but React's `useEffect` is deferred.\n\nFor the auto-upload case, the timing gap means Phoenix can't auto-upload. This is a known limitation of the current React upload hook implementation. Let me check if the Vue auto-upload test actually reliably passes or if it's also fragile.\n\nThe Vue test passes because `watchEffect` updates `data-phx-active-refs` synchronously during the reactive update cycle, so by the time Phoenix looks at the refs, they're already set.\n\nFor the React test, I should either:\n1. Fix the React hook to update refs synchronously (not via useEffect)\n2. Adjust the test to account for this limitation\n\nLet me fix the React hook - updating DOM attributes doesn't need to go through `useEffect`. I can do it directly in the render logic by using a ref callback or by updating the attributes immediately when the component receives new props.\n\nActually, the better fix is to update the `data-phx-active-refs` directly in `patchProps` or use `useLayoutEffect` instead of `useEffect` (which runs synchronously after DOM mutation but before paint)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1026,"cache_read_input_tokens":122772,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1026},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e05a5f27-3808-43b9-9b1f-a81d138cf285","uuid":"7a38b448-f7e6-4d5a-aa6f-8cbfb782b0f9"}
