{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018aP343oKj4VqAKLWPmtgVU","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# LiveVite Project Memory\n     2→\n     3→## Environment\n     4→- Node.js not in PATH directly; use `nix-shell -p nodejs --run \"...\"` for npm/npx commands\n     5→- `npm install` needed before tests (no node_modules checked in)\n     6→\n     7→## Architecture\n     8→- `assets/renderer.ts` - Framework renderer interface (`FrameworkRenderer`)\n     9→- `assets/renderers/vue.ts` - Vue implementation of FrameworkRenderer\n    10→- `assets/hooks.ts` - `getMultiRendererHook()` (multi-framework dispatch) + `getRendererHook()` (single-renderer shorthand) + `getVueHook()` (legacy Vue-specific)\n    11→- `assets/server.ts` - `getRendererRender()` (framework-agnostic SSR) + `getRender()` (legacy Vue SSR)\n    12→- All existing Vue APIs preserved for backward compatibility\n    13→- Elixir `live_vite.ex` renders `data-framework=\"vue\"` on component div\n    14→\n    15→## Key Patterns\n    16→- Hook stores renderer state as `this.vue` (even for non-Vue renderers, for backward compat)\n    17→- Hook stores active renderer as `this.__renderer` for use in updated/destroyed lifecycle\n    18→- `getMultiRendererHook(renderers)` dispatches based on `data-framework` DOM attribute\n    19→- Single-renderer fallback: if only one renderer registered, `data-framework` attribute is optional\n    20→- Slots flow as raw HTML strings to the renderer; renderer converts to framework-specific format\n    21→- Props parsed from DOM attributes are plain objects; renderer wraps in its reactivity system\n    22→- JSON Patch library (`jsonPatch.ts`) is framework-agnostic, operates on plain objects\n    23→- Elixir test failures for SSR NodeJS and installer tests are pre-existing (Node.js not in nix-shell PATH)\n    24→- E2E Vite build: run `npx vite build --config test/e2e/vite.config.js` from project root (not from test/e2e/)\n    25→- E2E test_helper.exs: needs `check_origin: false` and `<script type=\"module\">` for Playwright testing\n    26→- Playwright on NixOS: use `PLAYWRIGHT_CHROMIUM_EXECUTABLE_PATH` env var with nix chromium + `PLAYWRIGHT_SKIP_VALIDATE_HOST_REQUIREMENTS=1`\n    27→- `findComponent` updated to handle .vue/.tsx/.jsx/.ts/.js extensions (was .vue only)\n    28→- When using `getMultiRendererHook`, resolve functions must unwrap `.default` from ES module objects (unlike `createLiveVite` which does this automatically via `resolveComponent`)\n    29→- React slot props arrive as React elements (not functions) — render directly, don't call them\n    30→- E2E tests: 128 total (84 Vue + 44 React) all passing\n    31→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e05a5f27-3808-43b9-9b1f-a81d138cf285","uuid":"d787fde9-620b-4fe5-a765-d242402fb152","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/andre/.claude/projects/-home-andre-Documents-scratch-live-vue/memory/MEMORY.md","content":"# LiveVite Project Memory\n\n## Environment\n- Node.js not in PATH directly; use `nix-shell -p nodejs --run \"...\"` for npm/npx commands\n- `npm install` needed before tests (no node_modules checked in)\n\n## Architecture\n- `assets/renderer.ts` - Framework renderer interface (`FrameworkRenderer`)\n- `assets/renderers/vue.ts` - Vue implementation of FrameworkRenderer\n- `assets/hooks.ts` - `getMultiRendererHook()` (multi-framework dispatch) + `getRendererHook()` (single-renderer shorthand) + `getVueHook()` (legacy Vue-specific)\n- `assets/server.ts` - `getRendererRender()` (framework-agnostic SSR) + `getRender()` (legacy Vue SSR)\n- All existing Vue APIs preserved for backward compatibility\n- Elixir `live_vite.ex` renders `data-framework=\"vue\"` on component div\n\n## Key Patterns\n- Hook stores renderer state as `this.vue` (even for non-Vue renderers, for backward compat)\n- Hook stores active renderer as `this.__renderer` for use in updated/destroyed lifecycle\n- `getMultiRendererHook(renderers)` dispatches based on `data-framework` DOM attribute\n- Single-renderer fallback: if only one renderer registered, `data-framework` attribute is optional\n- Slots flow as raw HTML strings to the renderer; renderer converts to framework-specific format\n- Props parsed from DOM attributes are plain objects; renderer wraps in its reactivity system\n- JSON Patch library (`jsonPatch.ts`) is framework-agnostic, operates on plain objects\n- Elixir test failures for SSR NodeJS and installer tests are pre-existing (Node.js not in nix-shell PATH)\n- E2E Vite build: run `npx vite build --config test/e2e/vite.config.js` from project root (not from test/e2e/)\n- E2E test_helper.exs: needs `check_origin: false` and `<script type=\"module\">` for Playwright testing\n- Playwright on NixOS: use `PLAYWRIGHT_CHROMIUM_EXECUTABLE_PATH` env var with nix chromium + `PLAYWRIGHT_SKIP_VALIDATE_HOST_REQUIREMENTS=1`\n- `findComponent` updated to handle .vue/.tsx/.jsx/.ts/.js extensions (was .vue only)\n- When using `getMultiRendererHook`, resolve functions must unwrap `.default` from ES module objects (unlike `createLiveVite` which does this automatically via `resolveComponent`)\n- React slot props arrive as React elements (not functions) — render directly, don't call them\n- E2E tests: 128 total (84 Vue + 44 React) all passing\n","numLines":31,"startLine":1,"totalLines":31}}}
